### 2. SERVICE FILES PATTERNS
**Location:** `/home/saaln/cohort-003-project/app/services/`

All service files follow a consistent pattern:

**lessonService.ts (228 lines)** - Example implementation:
- **CRUD Operations:** `getLessonById()`, `getLessonsByModule()`, `createLesson()`, `updateLesson()`, `deleteLesson()`
- **Complex Updates:** Uses conditional logic to build updates object, only including fields that aren't null
- **Reordering Functions:** `moveLessonToPosition()`, `swapLessonPositions()`, `reorderLessons()`, `moveLessonToModule()`
- **Pattern:** Direct database calls using Drizzle ORM, no return-on-null for all operations

**Key Code Snippet:**
```typescript
export function updateLesson(
  id: number,
  title: string | null,
  content: string | null,
  videoUrl: string | null,
  durationMinutes: number | null,
  githubRepoUrl: string | null = null
) {
  const updates: Record<string, unknown> = {};
  if (title !== null) updates.title = title;
  if (content !== null) updates.content = content;
  if (videoUrl !== null) updates.videoUrl = videoUrl;
  if (durationMinutes !== null) updates.durationMinutes = durationMinutes;
  if (githubRepoUrl !== null) updates.githubRepoUrl = githubRepoUrl;

  if (Object.keys(updates).length === 0) {
    return getLessonById(id);
  }

  return db
    .update(lessons)
    .set(updates)
    .where(eq(lessons.id, id))
    .returning()
    .get();
}
```

**Other Core Services:**

- **courseService.ts (259 lines):** `getCourseById()`, `getCourseWithDetails()` (includes modules & lessons), filtering & search, status/price/PPP updates
- **moduleService.ts (153 lines):** Mirrors lesson service structure, handles course-level module operations
- **userService.ts (60 lines):** Simple CRUD for users, role management
- **enrollmentService.ts (154 lines):** Enrollment CRUD, duplicate prevention, course-student relationship queries
- **progressService.ts:** Tracks lesson completion status, calculates course progress
- **reviewService.ts (78 lines):** Course review creation/updates with upsert pattern

**reviewService Pattern (upsert):**
```typescript
export function createOrUpdateReview(
  userId: number,
  courseId: number,
  rating: number,
  body: string | null
) {
  const existing = getUserReviewForCourse(userId, courseId);
  if (existing) {
    db.update(courseReviews).set({ rating, body, updatedAt: new Date().toISOString() })
      .where(eq(courseReviews.id, existing.id)).run();
  } else {
    db.insert(courseReviews).values({ userId, courseId, rating, body }).run();
  }
}
```

